  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Set `output_determinism: advisory` on the `list-tasks` Action + the ADR-016 Reasoning tier + temperature ~0.2–0.3 (catalog data).</step>
    <step order="2">Declare the FR-03 bounded grounded-tool allow-list = {`spaarke.grid_overview`, `spaarke.daily_briefing_overview`} on the Action (the opt-in field from task 010).</step>
    <step order="3">Rewrite the `systemPrompt`: call `spaarke.grid_overview` (My-Tasks configId, OBO today) + `spaarke.daily_briefing_overview`, narrate a grounded summary (counts + top items, EACH cited to a tool result) + a recommendation, and open the Tasks surface — NOT the forbid-everything ack prompt.</step>
    <step order="4">Author/seed the Binding in `sprk_playbookconsumer` (disposition + `chipTransitions` for the E2 Briefing / Smart To Do follow-on cards).</step>
    <step order="5">Run `jps-validate` on the Action JSON.</step>
    <step order="6">Seed rows via `scripts/dataverse/Seed-PlaybookConsumers.ps1` (and the Action seed).</step>
    <step order="7">Build the nested-turn machinery (2026-08-16 scope addendum): (A) new `AdvisoryCapabilityRunner` (Services/Ai/Chat/) that runs a nested bounded turn constructing an `AgentToolFilterContext` with `AdvisoryToolAllowList` set (fires the task-011 PreFilter narrowing), streams the grounded+cited narration, and emits the `surface_launch` once; (B) route advisory + non-empty-allow-list dispatches to it from `SessionDispatchOrchestrator` (all other dispatches unchanged), threading `OutputDeterminism` + `GroundedToolAllowList` through the dispatch-path Action resolution.</step>
    <step order="8">Add unit + seam tests (tests/integration/seam/**): an advisory Action routes to the nested runner; a non-advisory Action does not; the nested turn mounts ONLY the allow-list end-to-end (no `BindingCapabilityTool`/refusal tool survives — the no-second-decider assertion). If the nested function-calling loop is rejected at adr-check/code-review as a second probabilistic surface, implement fallback A′ (deterministic in-code tool calls + ONE advisory completion).</step>
    <step order="9">dotnet build + publish size check (COMPRESSED ≤60 MB; baseline 44.96 MB) + CVE scan; run `jps-validate`; /conflict-check before the PR; update TASK-INDEX ✅.</step>
  </steps>
  <escalation>
    <trigger>If authoring the advisory capability appears to require a second decider / classifier / routing surface (beyond the task 011 deterministic pre-filter) to select the two tools, STOP and escalate (ADR-039 forbids it) rather than adding dispatch logic.</trigger>
  </escalation>
  <justification>
    <existing>`list-tasks` (ack-only) Action + Binding already exist — the exact P1-defect path ("what do I need to do today" → thin ack).</existing>
    <extension>Upgrade `list-tasks` to advisory + bounded tools (reuse the two shipped grounded tools + the one decider) — no new executor, no net-new tool.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>"what do I need to do today" stays a thin ack with no grounded summary or recommendation — the P1 defect persists.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>
  <outputs>
    <output type="config">infra/dataverse/actions/list-tasks.action.json (upgraded to advisory + Reasoning tier + temp + bounded allow-list + rewritten systemPrompt)</output>
    <output type="config">infra/dataverse/sprk_playbookconsumer-rows.json (task-agenda Binding row + chipTransitions)</output>
  </outputs>
  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">The P1 DoD passes: "what do I need to do today" → grounded summary (real counts/top items, each cited) + a recommendation + Tasks opens.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The Action row carries `output_determinism: advisory` + the ADR-016 Reasoning tier + temperature ~0.2–0.3.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Only {`spaarke.grid_overview`, `spaarke.daily_briefing_overview`} mount for the capability's turn.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Every narrated number is cited to a tool result; no fabrication (negative case).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The Tasks surface opens once — no duplicate tab.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The Binding carries `chipTransitions` so E2 Briefing / Smart To Do follow-on cards can key off this capability.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A new `AdvisoryCapabilityRunner` runs the nested bounded turn (setting `AgentToolFilterContext.AdvisoryToolAllowList` → the task-011 PreFilter fires); `SessionDispatchOrchestrator` routes advisory + non-empty-allow-list Actions to it and leaves all other dispatches unchanged (`OutputDeterminism` + `GroundedToolAllowList` threaded through the dispatch-path Action resolution).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Seam coverage (tests/integration/seam/**) proves: advisory Action → nested runner; non-advisory → unchanged linear path; the nested turn mounts ONLY the allow-list end-to-end and NO capability/refusal tool survives (no-second-decider, ADR-039).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`jps-validate` passes green.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">If BFF code touched: publish ≤60 MB reported (absolute + delta); no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
  <notes>This UPGRADES the existing ack-only `list-tasks` Action/Binding — the P1 defect is specifically on that path. Both grounded tools already exist and are shipped; do not author net-new tools. Depends on task 010 (opt-in field) + task 011 (pre-filter narrowing). /conflict-check with compose-r5/r6 + assistant-r3 before the PR.</notes>
